// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every index from the insertion point to the previous size of the list, the element at each subsequent index is either null and was null before, or is equal to the element that was at the current index before the insertion.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from the insertion point to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at this position was null, or it is equal to the old element at this position.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is valid (between 0 and the size of the list inclusive), then for every position from the index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at that position is null, or it is equal to the old element at that position.
--------------------
